 *   https://docs.midnight.network/guides/security-best-practices
 *   section "Restricting a circuit to a group"
 *
 * Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#902
 * Auto-synced Compact reference pages still do not warn that ownPublicKey()
 * is a prover-controlled witness. This lab source is that warning for the
 * group pattern. It does not edit midnight-docs and is not a public deploy.
 *
 * Related open gap: midnightntwrk/servicedesk#202 (kernel.caller is undefined).
 * Binding path.leaf to derivePublicKey(secretKey()) is the documented local
 * substitute. This file does not invent kernel.caller.
 *
 * Language pin: Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
 * LOCAL-TRUE. Source only until the next compact compile. Not deployed.
